<title>MEXICO: Cotton production in Mexico's Durango state slumps.</title>
<headline>Cotton production in Mexico's Durango state slumps.</headline>
<dateline>GUADALAJARA, Mexico 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cotton production in the Mexican state of Durango has slumped this year because of drought, a state official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Alvaro Torres Vargas, deputy secretary for rural development in the central state, said output was expected to fall to 18,000 tonnes in 1996 from 26,000 tonnes last year.</p>
<p>&quot;Because of the drought, because the reservoirs have very little water, there was very little cotton, he said.</p>
<p>He said Durango was Mexico's seventh largest cotton producing state.</p>
<p>--Veronica Galan, Guadalajara newsroom, +523 817-0397</p>
